<h1>Topics — where each pressure-test lives</h1>
<p class="lede">A wayfinding index only. The thirteen pressure-tests by their plain names, with links to where each is defined, debated, drawn, and measured. Nothing is claimed on this page that is not already on the pages it points to.</p>
<p>Throughout the record the thirteen carry short codes — <strong>M</strong> for the master condition, <strong>D1–D4</strong> the drivers, <strong>Y1–Y4</strong> the dynamics, <strong>S1–S4</strong> the symptoms.</p>
<p class="companion-note">Every topic below is: defined in <a href="{{ '/docs/goals/' | url }}">Goals</a> · debated in <a href="{{ '/panel/session_2_pressure_tests/' | url }}">Session 2</a> · its arrows drawn in <a href="{{ '/docs/pressure_tests_causal_hypothesis/' | url }}">the causal hypothesis</a> · its status measured on <a href="{{ '/diagrams/' | url }}">Self-audit &amp; figures</a>.</p>
<p class="companion-note">Care is not one of the thirteen. The record says so itself: <a href="{{ '/docs/episode_unit/' | url }}">the repair-episode unit</a> names maintenance-shaped repair — care systems, mutual aid — as a structural blind spot still uncut ("the invisible load-bearing wall" — Le Guin, preserved in dissent), and <a href="{{ '/panel/session_2_pressure_tests/' | url }}">Session 2</a> keeps the objection that named care work on the record (D-005).</p>
